section start
title start
Focus box types
title end

paragraph start
todo: open notation requires a title for every box type
So that focus level 2 can show a title for each box type, the notation system has to require a title for every box type. This changes AIU NOTATION, a sibling folder, so it is a decision to take there and not a patch from the editor. Owner request 2026-11-01.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Tab management and the key table
title end

paragraph start
todo: tab management needs more features. There is no workspace management, no project management and no keys for them. These need real work: open, switch, close and list workspaces and projects, each with keys. Owner request 2026-11-02.
todo: the mode line shows the available keys but only the keys alone. It needs a full table of every key with what it does, per layer. Owner request 2026-11-02.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
INSANELY IMPORTANT: the .aiu-memory file
title end

paragraph start
todo: a .aiu-memory file kept in the directory the owner works in (workspace or project). It remembers the open tabs, workspaces and projects, so nothing is lost when aiutd exits and everything comes back when it is opened in that directory again. Owner request 2026-11-02, top priority.
todo: feature 1 of .aiu-memory: the work placement is never lost on exit. Open tabs, their order, the current tab, the cursor and view place of each, and the open workspaces and projects are saved and restored.
todo: feature 2 of .aiu-memory: workspace settings. A directory or workspace can say which projects it holds and which files and tabs open by themselves when aiutd starts there. The format and the rules need thinking first: where the file lives, what it holds, and how it relates to the plain text .aiu format. It must not use .org files and must not edit AIU NOTATION.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
URGENT: file manager in AIU ECOSYSTEM / FILE MANAGER/
title end

paragraph start
todo: clone https://github.com/Canop/broot and https://github.com/alexpasmantier/television into AIU ECOSYSTEM/ FILE MANAGER/.
todo: combine them into one file manager, then add oil.nvim style editing: the directory is edited as a text buffer and saving applies the renames, moves, deletes and creates.
todo: make aiutd use this file manager.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
AFTER THE FILE BREAKING: keys, folders and one test per file
title end

paragraph start
todo: first check that the keybindings are set properly.
todo: then sort the files into subfolders by subject. Many files share a subject and sit loose in one folder, so each subject gets its own subdirectory.
todo: after that, move the key sets into their categories: the keys for tabs go in the tabs folder, and so on, so no key has to be hunted for.
todo: move the test files the same way. Every file gets its own test file from that point, so the mechanic can test each file properly.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
AIU NOTATION files carry notation in their names
title end

paragraph start
todo: every file of the editor that belongs to AIU NOTATION (its modules, checks, tests and docs) gets notation in its file name, because these files sit in many folders. Then one search for notation finds all of them when AIU NOTATION is updated. Do not edit AIU NOTATION itself.
todo: do this together with the subject subfolders, and keep the one-way rule: the editor requires the notation files, never the other way round.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Still to do: tests, gate and tui leftovers
title end

paragraph start
todo: test system per-frame state line. The test system should show the editor state on each frame, so a failed test says what the state was at every step.
todo: Rust tests in the gate. The Rust side of the editor gets its own tests, run by the gate stages like the Racket ones.
todo: errortrace run. Run the editor under errortrace once and fix what it finds. The details are in plan.md.
todo: gutter files. gutter.rkt and gutterview.rkt are loose in editor/tui. Give the gutter its own folder, and give each file its own test file.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
ONE-WAY LINT CHECKS NOTHING
title end
paragraph start
todo: the one-way lint prints NOTHING-TO-CHECK, so it enforces nothing. Find why it sees no Racket files (the project path holds the letter AE), put tui into its area table at its true place (entry and routes already require tui, and the key tables now live in tui folders), and make it fail for real on an upward require.
paragraph end
section end

